      "reason": [
        "The sink region is the Result-unwrapped Vec returned by map_matching_items and used as the receiver of .remove(0), not a logging macro or a log-writing call.",
        "The exact analysis pack source a7057b836bf29767461026718b14d20790b9085f models <alloc::vec::Vec>::remove Argument[self] as log-injection (rust.model.yml line 8767); CleartextLoggingExtensions.qll consumes this sink kind.",
        "Rust 1.95.0 Vec::remove accepts unconstrained T, returns the removed element and only formats the integer index and integer length on bounds failure; neither remove nor try_remove formats or writes any Vec element.",
        "map_matching_items requires uniqueness here: zero matches return NoEntry, multiple matches return Ambiguous, one successful callback produces one element; its legacy fallback has the same count checks. The successful flow cannot reach a bounds failure at index 0.",
        "The generic mapper yields different T for set_secret/get_password/get_secret/new_from_item. SARIF combines callback flows (including Result<()> from set_item_secret and password decoding in a metadata-only new_from_matching_item instantiation); these cross-instantiation paths do not establish a secret-to-log operation."
      ],
      "limits": [
        "This classifies only the exact three SARIF results from b58d870a2c38ebee0aa0b974d9f03767c888fa7e, not all logging in keyring or the rest of the repository.",
